# Spaces and owners

A document is only as trustworthy as the person known to keep it true.

| Kind | What it is | Must have | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Workspace** | An area a role keeps current, under `docs/`. Either a **project workspace** (baseline, architecture, product, delivery, quality) or a **layer workspace** (backend, frontend, design, and any layer this project adds). | `README.md` (index) and `CLAUDE.md` (owner, scope, rules). No `decisions/` folder — records live in `docs/decisions/`. | Exactly one named person. |
| **Supporting folder** | Everything else: glossary, conventions, plugins. | Nothing extra. No `CLAUDE.md`. | The repository owner. |

- **One space, one owner.** Two names means nobody is accountable when they disagree.
  One person may own several spaces. Unassigned means the repository owner, never
  nobody.
- The owner keeps the space at the state of today, is the **default reviewer** of every
  change under it, and keeps its `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` true.
- Owners are named as `Full Name (e-mail)`. The area map in
  [docs/README.md](../docs/README.md) is authoritative; a workspace `CLAUDE.md` repeats
  only its own owner. Change both in the same change.
- **Repository owner:** {{OWNER}}.

## Workspace `CLAUDE.md` shape

```markdown
# <Space> workspace

**Owner:** <Full name> (<e-mail>) — default reviewer for changes here.

## Scope
- What belongs here; what does not, and where it lives instead.

## Rules for this space
- Only rules a newcomer would get wrong.

## Start here
- The README and the one document a task here begins with.
```

## Adding a workspace

Create the folder under `docs/` with `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, and add its row to the
area map in the same change. With the shared plugin installed,
`/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared:{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-space` does both and cannot forget the row.

A layer this project does not have yet — `mobile`, `platform`, anything else — becomes
a workspace the moment it has content, never before.
